{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id494479509"}, "name":{"label":"ainsler"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-10-21T01:59:12-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0.98"}, "id":{"label":"14692466147"}, "title":{"label":"Too much change"}, "content":{"label":"This game used to be a lot of fun, but the recent changes have taken away much of what made it enjoyable. The game is full of  bots that don’t behave in a balanced or rewarding way.\n\nThe biggest issue, though, is matchmaking. Teams frequently feel uneven, and it’s common to finish in the top three while still losing game after game. Losing 10 matches in a row despite consistently performing well makes it feel like individual effort has very little impact on the outcome.\n\nAir Superiority also seems to place much more emphasis on kills than capturing objectives. That shift discourages objective-based gameplay and makes the mode feel less strategic than it used to. This is across all game modes with the exception of team death match.\n\nOn top of the gameplay issues, the monetization has become increasingly aggressive. It often feels like the game is constantly pushing players to spend more money rather than focusing on improving the overall experience. The game still has a strong foundation, but right now it feels like profit has become a higher priority than balanced, enjoyable gameplay.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1461423243&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
